<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n920" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">admŏnĭtus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		admoneo, used only in the abl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A reminding</i>, <i>suggestion</i>
			(class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acrius de claris viris locorum admonitu
					cogitamus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 5, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. R. A. 729</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">admonitu Allobrogum praetorem misi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 3, 3, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3, 612</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				3, 92</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 4,
				13, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3,
			81</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Instance</i>, <i>request</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">admonitu tuo perfeci libros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 13, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut Attici admonitu eam reficiendam curaret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Att.
					20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 48</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Reproof</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acrior admonitu est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 564</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
